Package: Loupe2R
Type: Package
Title: Import 10x Genomics Visium '.cloupe' Files into Seurat Objects
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Niel", "Infante", email = "nielinfante@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Extracts count matrices, spatial coordinates, tissue images, UMAP
    embeddings, and cluster labels from 10x Genomics .cloupe files (including
    Visium HD) and imports them into Seurat objects via a Python extraction
    step (reticulate). Requires Python with numpy, scipy, Pillow, and a local
    installation of the cellgeni/cloupe package (not bundled; see
    'SystemRequirements').
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    Seurat (>= 5.0.0),
    SeuratObject,
    methods,
    reticulate,
    png,
    jsonlite,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr,
    rmarkdown,
    arrow,
    digest,
    withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with numpy, scipy, Pillow; the
    cellgeni/cloupe Python package (AGPL-3.0, https://github.com/cellgeni/cloupe),
    installed separately by the user and referenced via set_cloupe_path() or
    options(loupe2r.cloupe_pkg = ...) -- NOT bundled with or distributed by
    this R package.
